WEBVTT

00:00:00.700 --> 00:00:10.600
AI agents can write code and move money. But a payment rail cannot tell whether
an offchain pull request truly met its scope.

00:00:11.000 --> 00:00:21.600
ScopeSettle locks the rubric, weights, provider, budget, expiry, and confidence threshold
before funding an ERC-8183 escrow on X Layer.

00:00:22.000 --> 00:00:33.600
The Testnet deliverable is pinned to one GitHub pull request and one immutable head commit.
No moving branch can change the evidence.

00:00:34.000 --> 00:00:46.600
Deterministic checks verify identity, required files, diff bounds, and CI.
The hosted evaluator scores only cited evidence against the immutable rubric.

00:00:47.000 --> 00:00:59.600
The manifest criterion scored 100, but the required lockfile criterion scored zero
because pinned CI was failing. Weighted score: 50.

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:11.600
Uncertainty did not trigger an automatic payout. A named trusted reviewer rejected
the verdict and refunded the full valueless Testnet escrow.

00:01:12.000 --> 00:01:21.600
The contracts are also source-verified on X Layer Mainnet with native USDC.
No Mainnet job or user adoption is claimed.

00:01:22.000 --> 00:01:29.500
Every report, hash, receipt, limitation, and test is public.
ScopeSettle: verified work, automatic settlement.
